    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm also curious about the volume side of things. If I decide to implement a periodized approach, should I be looking to decrease intensity while increasing volume to stimulate more hypertrophy, or is it better to stick to higher intensity to keep the CNS primed? I want to make sure I'm not just spinning my wheels.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Increasing volume while maintaining moderate intensity is generally more effective for stimulating hypertrophy compared to simply adding weight with low volume, as it provides the necessary mechanical tension and metabolic stress across a larger number of repetitions. This approach respects the CNS limitations of a plateau by ensuring high-quality training quality without excessive fatigue accumulation. Ultimately, a periodized plan likely combines both phases strategically rather than relying on a single method to overcome the stagnation in strength and muscle growth.",
      "source": "target",
